WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.640
Luke 13. There were some present at that very time who told him about the Galileans whose blood

00:08.640 --> 00:15.520
Pilate had mingled with their sacrifices. And he answered them, Do you think that these Galileans

00:15.520 --> 00:21.320
were worse sinners than all the other Galileans, because they suffered in this way? No, I tell you,

00:21.560 --> 00:27.800
but unless you repent, you will all likewise perish. Or those eighteen on whom the tower

00:27.800 --> 00:33.620
in Siloam fell and killed them, do you think that they were worse offenders than all the others who

00:33.620 --> 00:40.620
lived in Jerusalem? No, I tell you, but unless you repent, you will all likewise perish.

00:41.120 --> 00:47.180
And he told this parable. A man had a fig tree planted in his vineyard, and he came seeking

00:47.180 --> 00:53.580
fruit on it and found none. And he said to the vinedresser, Look, for three years now I have

00:53.580 --> 00:57.300
come seeking fruit on this fig tree, and I find none. Cut it down.

00:57.800 --> 01:04.060
Why should it use up the ground? And he answered him, Sir, let it alone this year also,

01:04.380 --> 01:08.840
until I dig around it and put on manure. Then, if it should bear fruit next year,

01:08.840 --> 01:12.180
well and good. But if not, you can cut it down.

01:13.960 --> 01:19.120
Now he was teaching in one of the synagogues on the Sabbath, and there was a woman who had had a

01:19.120 --> 01:24.900
disabling spirit for eighteen years. She was bent over and could not fully straighten herself.

01:25.620 --> 01:27.780
When Jesus saw her, he called her to the synagogue, and she was there. And she was there, and she was

01:27.800 --> 01:32.280
there, and she was there. And he called her over and said to her, Woman, you are freed from your

01:32.280 --> 01:37.940
disability. And he laid his hands on her, and immediately she was made straight, and she

01:37.940 --> 01:44.340
glorified God. But the ruler of the synagogue, indignant because Jesus had healed on the Sabbath,

01:44.860 --> 01:52.040
said to the people, There are six days in which work ought to be done. Come on those days and be

01:52.040 --> 01:57.280
healed, and not on the Sabbath day. Then the Lord answered him,

01:57.800 --> 02:03.540
You hypocrites! Does not each of you on the Sabbath untie his ox or his donkey from the

02:03.540 --> 02:10.400
manger, and lead it away to water it? And ought not this woman, a daughter of Abraham, whom Satan

02:10.400 --> 02:15.180
bound for eighteen years, be loosed from this bond on the Sabbath day?

02:15.900 --> 02:20.860
As he said these things, all his adversaries were put to shame, and all the people rejoiced at all

02:20.860 --> 02:27.320
the glorious things that were done by him. He said, Therefore, What is the kingdom of God like?

02:27.800 --> 02:33.200
And to what shall I compare it? It is like a grain of mustard seed that a man took and

02:33.200 --> 02:39.020
sowed in his garden, and it grew and became a tree, and the birds of the air made nests in

02:39.020 --> 02:46.180
its branches. And again he said, To what shall I compare the kingdom of God? It is like leaven

02:46.180 --> 02:51.360
that a woman took and hid in three measures of flour, until it was all leavened.

02:52.980 --> 02:57.700
He went on his way through towns and villages, teaching and journeying toward Jerusalem.

02:57.800 --> 03:03.340
And someone said to him, Lord, will those who are saved be few?

03:03.960 --> 03:10.160
And he said to them, Strive to enter through the narrow door, for many, I tell you, will seek to

03:10.160 --> 03:15.600
enter and will not be able. When once the master of the house is risen and shut the door, and you

03:15.600 --> 03:21.880
begin to stand outside and to knock at the door, saying, Lord, open to us, then he will answer you,

03:22.020 --> 03:25.800
I do not know where you come from. Then you will begin to say,

03:26.240 --> 03:27.780
We ate and drank in your house. And he will answer you, I do not know where you come from.

03:27.780 --> 03:32.780
We ate and drank in your presence, and you taught in our streets. But he will say, I tell you,

03:32.980 --> 03:37.860
I do not know where you come from. Depart from me, all you workers of evil.

03:39.020 --> 03:45.400
In that place there will be weeping and gnashing of teeth, when you see Abraham and Isaac and

03:45.400 --> 03:51.220
Jacob, and all the prophets in the kingdom of God, but you yourselves cast out. And people

03:51.220 --> 03:57.660
will come from east and west, and from north and south, and recline at table in the kingdom of God.

03:57.780 --> 04:04.080
And behold, some are last who will be first, and some are first who will be last.

04:04.800 --> 04:07.660
At that very hour some Pharisees came and said to him,

04:08.360 --> 04:12.640
Get away from here, for Herod wants to kill you. And he said to them,

04:13.360 --> 04:19.640
Go and tell that fox, Behold, I cast out demons and perform cures today and tomorrow,

04:20.000 --> 04:25.980
and the third day I finish my course. Nevertheless, I must go on my way today and tomorrow,

04:25.980 --> 04:27.600
and the day following.

04:28.040 --> 04:31.620
For it cannot be that a prophet should perish away from Jerusalem.

04:32.900 --> 04:39.960
O Jerusalem, Jerusalem, the city that kills the prophets and stones those who are sent to it,

04:40.360 --> 04:43.600
how often would I have gathered your children together,

04:44.160 --> 04:48.820
as a hen gathers her brood under her wings, and you would not.

04:49.880 --> 04:55.660
Behold, your house is forsaken, and I tell you, you will not see me until you say,

04:55.960 --> 04:57.660
Blessed is he who cometh.

04:57.780 --> 04:59.520
He who comes in the name of the Lord.

